From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chromium meta-browser maintainers <meta-browser@lists.openembedded.org>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] v8: disable trap-only UBSan hardening without runtime

The scarthgap system Clang cannot use Chromium's newer
fsanitize-ignore-for-ubsan-feature option. Without that option, the
trap-only array-bounds and return configs make V8 report sanitizer features
as enabled while the sanitizer runtime is not linked. This is especially
problematic for mksnapshot, which is executed through QEMU during the build.

Keep the configs available for real sanitizer builds, but remove them from
normal V8 targets when no sanitizer runtime is being used.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [OE-specific]
---
 v8/gni/v8.gni | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/v8/gni/v8.gni b/v8/gni/v8.gni
--- a/v8/gni/v8.gni
+++ b/v8/gni/v8.gni
@@ -395,6 +395,15 @@
   v8_path_prefix + ":strict_warnings",
 ]
 
+# The system Clang build does not provide the sanitizer runtime used by these
+# trap-only hardening configs. In particular, mksnapshot is executed during
+# the build, so a trap in it aborts snapshot generation under QEMU.
+if (is_clang && !using_sanitizer) {
+  v8_remove_configs += [
+    "//build/config/compiler:sanitize_c_array_bounds",
+    "//build/config/compiler:sanitize_return",
+  ]
+}
 if (v8_force_optimize_speed) {
   # Switch to force -O3 optimization regardless of platform or sanitizer
   # usage.
-- 
2.54.0
